# NOTICE — zoinks

This project, `zoinks`, is a Python + Rust port of Pablo Stanley's
[`yoinks`](https://github.com/pablostanley/yoinks) TypeScript TUI
([MIT-licensed](https://github.com/pablostanley/yoinks/blob/master/LICENSE)).

## What was ported from `yoinks`

The following were directly translated (with permission under the MIT
license) from the original `yoinks` TypeScript source by Pablo Stanley:

- **Overall UX flow** — the input → probing → picking → downloading → done
  phase machine, including the specific keyboard shortcuts (`^t` for theme,
  `↑`/`↓` or `j`/`k` for picker, `esc` back, `^c` quit).
- **Tagline & copy** — "yoink any video. paste. yoink. done." and the
  footer-hint wording.
- **Block-character logo** — the 3-row ASCII art logo
  (`▓ ▓ █▀█ ▀█▀ █▀▄█ █ █ █▀▀` / `▀█▀ █ ▓  ▓  █  ▓ ▓▀▄ ▀▀▓` /
  ` ▀  ▀▀▀ ▀▀▀ ▀  ▀ ▀ ▀ ▀▀▀`) ships verbatim.
- **Theme palette** — the exact `#18181b` / `#52525b` / `#a1a1aa` / `#ffffff`
  hex values for `light` and `dark` modes.
- **Platform detection table** — the YouTube / X / Instagram / Threads /
  TikTok / Vimeo / Twitch / Reddit / Facebook host list.
- **yt-dlp wrapper logic** — the `ensure_yt_dlp` (download-or-reuse)
  strategy, the `build_choices` height-cap + audio-only-mp3 picker, the
  `YOINK|...` progress wire format, and the cached-info.json fast-path +
  retry-on-failure flow.
- **Storage layout** — `~/.<name>/bin` for the bundled yt-dlp,
  `~/.config/<name>/history.json` for the URL history (capped at 50,
  deduped).
- **Logo and screenshot assets** — `assets/logo-light.svg`,
  `assets/logo-dark.svg`, `assets/home.png`, `assets/download-options.png`
  are byte-for-byte copies of the originals.
- **MIT license** — preserved.

## What is new in `zoinks`

- **PyO3 bindings** exposing the Rust core as a Python module
  (`zoinks._zoinks_core`), installable via `pip install zoinks`.
- **Textual-based Python TUI** (`python/zoinks/tui/app.py`) — a parallel
  implementation to the Rust ratatui TUI, driven by the same Rust core.
- **`--cookies <file>` flag** — pass a Netscape-format cookies file to
  yt-dlp for sites that require login (X, Facebook, Instagram).
- **`--update` / `-U` flag** — refresh the bundled yt-dlp binary on
  demand.
- **Auto-update on `Unsupported URL`** — if yt-dlp rejects a URL, zoinks
  runs `yt-dlp -U` and retries automatically (handles the case where
  the bundled yt-dlp is a few weeks out of date and a site shipped a
  new URL scheme, e.g., X's 19-digit snowflake IDs).
- **Auto-retry on download failure** — if the cached media URLs expire,
  zoinks retries once with a fresh probe (the Rust TUI now matches the
  Python TUI's behaviour).
- **Permissive format selector** — falls back through 6 alternatives
  instead of 4, with the ultimate `b` always matching.
- **Actionable error messages** — known patterns (`Unsupported URL`,
  `No video formats found`, `Requested format is not available`,
  `login required`, `429 Too Many Requests`) get a one-line hint about
  what to do.
- **`yt_dlp_version_is_recent` check** — refuses to use a system yt-dlp
  older than 2024.0 (silently out-of-date system installs were the
  root cause of the original "Unsupported URL" / "No video formats"
  failures).

